<title>UK: Murray Income Trust sells U.S. portfolio.</title>
<headline>Murray Income Trust sells U.S. portfolio.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Murray Income Trust Plc said on Wednesday that it decided in December to sell the remainder of its U.S. portfolio as part of its policy in reducing its overseas investment.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement accompanying its first half results that the proceeds of the U.S. portfolio sale will be re-invested in UK equities.</p>
<p>It said it was cautious on the prospects for the UK equity market and will concentrate on long term fundemental prospects.</p>
<p>Murray's net asset value per share increased to 409.5p in the six months to December 31, 1996, versus 376.2p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
